":"2009","note":"Learning Theory 2006","issn":"0022-0000","doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcss.2008.07.003","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022000008000652","author":"Maria-Florina Balcan and Alina Beygelzimer and John Langford","keywords":"Active learning, Agnostic setting, Sample complexity, Linear separators","abstract":"We state and analyze the first active learning algorithm that finds an ϵ-optimal hypothesis in any hypothesis class, when the underlying distribution has arbitrary forms of noise. The algorithm, A2 (for Agnostic Active), relies only upon the assumption that it has access to a stream of unlabeled examples drawn i.i.d. from a fixed distribution. We show that A2 achieves an exponential improvement (i.e., requires only O(ln1ϵ) samples to find an ϵ-optimal classifier) over the usual sample complexity of supervised learning, for several settings considered before in the realizable case. These include learning threshold classifiers and learning homogeneous linear separators with respect to an input distribution which is uniform over the unit sphere."},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Blondeletal2008","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"841d884d0d8e4ee1","fields":{"author":"Blondel, V. D. and Guillaume, J. L. and Lambiotte, R. and Lefebvre, E.","title":"Fast unfolding of communities in large networks","journal":"J. Stat. Mech.-Theory Exp.","volume":"2008","year":"2008","pages":"P10008"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Brown1992","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Brown, Peter and Della Pietra, Stephen and Pietra, Vincent and Lai, Jenifer and Mercer, Robert","year":"1992","month":"01","pages":"31-40","title":"An Estimate of an Upper Bound for the Entropy of English","volume":"18","journal":"Computational Linguistics"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Brown1993","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Brown, Peter and Della Pietra, Stephen and Pietra, Vincent and Mercer, Robert","year":"1993","month":"01","pages":"263-311","title":"The Mathematics of Statistical Machine Translation: Parameter Estimation","volume":"19","journal":"Computational Linguistics"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Chenetal2013","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Chen, Q. and Wu, T. T. and Fang, M.","title":"Detecting local community structure in complex networks based on local degree central nodes","journal":"Physica A.","volume":"392","year":"2013","pages":"529-537"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Clausetetal2004","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"189128a811b8d09c","fields":{"author":"Clauset, A. and Newman, M. E. J. and Moore, C.","title":"Finding community structure in very large networks","journal":"Phys. Rev. E.","volume":"70","year":"2004","pages":"066111"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Cohn94improvinggeneralization","verdict":"partial","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"2be2d8618eae4ede","fields":{"author":"David Cohn and Richard Ladner and Alex Waibel","title":"Improving generalization with active learning","booktitle":"Machine Learning","year":"1994","pages":"201--221"},"diffs":[{"field":"authors","in_document":"David Cohn and Richard Ladner and Alex Waibel","in_source":"David Cohn and Les Atlas and Richard Ladner","severity":"high"}]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"DAGAN1995150","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"title":"Committee-Based Sampling For Training Probabilistic Classifiers","editor":"Armand Prieditis and Stuart Russell","booktitle":"Machine Learning Proceedings 1995","publisher":"Morgan Kaufmann","address":"San Francisco (CA)","pages":"150-157","year":"1995","isbn":"978-1-55860-377-6","doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-1-55860-377-6.50027-X","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B978155860377650027X","author":"Ido Dagan and Sean P. Engelson","abstract":"In many real-world learning tasks, it is expensive to acquire a sufficient number of labeled examples for training. This paper proposes a general method for efficiently training probabilistic classifiers, by selecting for training only the more informative examples in a stream of unlabeled examples. The method, committee-based sampling, evaluates the informativeness of an example by measuring the degree of disagreement between several model variants. These variants (the committee) are drawn randomly from a probability distribution conditioned by the training set selected so far (Monte-Carlo sampling). The method is particularly attractive because it evaluates the expected information gain from a training example implicitly, making the model both easy to implement and generally applicable. We further show how to apply committee-based sampling for training Hidden Markov Model classifiers, which are commonly used for complex classification tasks. The method was implemented and tested for the task of tagging words in natural language sentences with parts-of-speech. Experimental evaluation of committee-based sampling versus standard sequential training showed a substantial improvement in training efficiency."},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Danonetal2005","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"ac32da8571b72c18","fields":{"author":"Danon, L. and Diaz-Guilera, A. and Duch, J. and Arenas, A.","title":"Comparing community structure identification","journal":"J. Stat. Mech.-Theory Exp.","volume":"","year":"2005","pages":"P09008"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Eck2008_1000010682","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Eck, Matthias","year":"2008","title":"Developing Deployable Spoken Language Translation Systems given Limited Resources","doi":"10.5445/IR/1000010682","publisher":"{Universität Karlsruhe (TH)}","keywords":"Spoken Language Translation, Low Cost Portability, Mobile Devices","language":"english"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Fabioetal2013","verdict":"partial","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"c24d9606d3bad1c7","fields":{"author":"Fabio, D. R. and Fabio, D. and Carlo, P.","title":"Profiling core-periphery network structure by random walkers","journal":"Sci. Rep.","volume":"3","year":"2013","pages":"1467"},"diffs":[{"field":"authors","in_document":"Fabio, D. R. and Fabio, D. and Carlo, P.","in_source":"Fabio Della Rossa and Fabio Dercole and Carlo Piccardi","severity":"high"}]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"FabricioLiang2013","verdict":"partial","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"4cefaad91e46ea29","fields":{"author":"Fabricio, B. and Liang, Z.","title":"Fuzzy community structure detection by 