ages":"112--122","abstract":"This paper describes Facebook AI{'}s submission to the WAT 2019 Myanmar-English translation task. Our baseline systems are BPE-based transformer models. We explore methods to leverage monolingual data to improve generalization, including self-training, back-translation and their combination. We further improve results by using noisy channel re-ranking and ensembling. We demonstrate that these techniques can significantly improve not only a system trained with additional monolingual data, but even the baseline system trained exclusively on the provided small parallel dataset. Our system ranks first in both directions according to human evaluation and BLEU, with a gain of over 8 BLEU points above the second best system."},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"class_C_finite_harm","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Juhas, A. and Novak, L.A.","journal":"Microwave Theory and Techniques, IEEE Transactions on","title":"Comments on \"Class-E, Class-C, and Class-F Power Amplifier Based Upon a Finite Number of Harmonics\"","year":"2009","month":"june","volume":"57","number":"6","pages":"1623 -1625","keywords":"class-C power amplifier;class-E power amplifier;class-F power amplifier;finite harmonic;harmonic analysis;power amplifiers;","doi":"10.1109/TMTT.2009.2019999","issn":"0018-9480"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"class_c_drive_shape","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Zivkovic-Dzunja, Z. and Markovic, A.","journal":"Broadcasting, IEEE Transactions on","title":"THE Drive-Wave Shape Influence on the Class C Tuned HF H