rical Methods in Natural Language Processing","month":"sep","year":"2015","address":"Lisbon, Portugal","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"https://aclanthology.org/D15-1166","doi":"10.18653/v1/D15-1166","pages":"1412--1421"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"lut_predistortion","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"71048ef8545afca1","fields":{"author":"Muhonen, K.J. and Kavehrad, M. and Krishnamoorthy, R.","journal":"Vehicular Technology, IEEE Transactions on","title":"Look-up table techniques for adaptive digital predistortion: a development and comparison","year":"2000","month":"sep","volume":"49","number":"5","pages":"1995 -2002","keywords":"BER;adaptive digital predistortion;adaptive indexing;amplifier efficiency;bit error rate;constellation distortion;in-band distortion;look-up table techniques;nonuniform spacing technique;out-of-band distortion;performance;performance evaluation;spectral regrowth analysis;UHF power amplifiers;digital radio;land mobile radio;linearisation techniques;radio transmitters;spectral analysis;table lookup;","doi":"10.1109/25.892601","issn":"0018-9545"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"miguel_conference","verdict":"partial","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"dad79edac963936e","fields":{"author":"Rodr\\'iguez, M. and Roberg, M. and Pack, R. and Fernandez, P. and Popovi\\'c, Z. and Alarcon E. and Maksimovi\\'c, D.","booktitle":"Power Electronics and Motion Control Conference, 2012. EPE-PEMC 2012 ECCE Europe. 15th International","title":"Resonant pulse-shaping power supply for radar transmitters","year":"2012","month":"","volume":"","number":"","pages":"","keywords":"","note":"","doi":"","issn":""},"diffs":[{"field":"authors","in_document":"Rodr\\'iguez, M. and Roberg, M. and Pack, R. and Fernandez, P. and Popovi\\'c, Z. and Alarcon E. and Maksimovi\\'c, D.","in_source":"Miguel Rodriguez and Michael Roberg and Riley Pack and Pablo Fernandez and Eduard Alarcon and Zoya Popovic and Dragan Maksimovic","severity":"high"}]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"murthy-etal-2019-addressing","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"71048ef8545afca1","fields":{"title":"Addressing word-order Divergence in Multilingual Neural Machine Translation for extremely Low Resource Languages","author":"Murthy, Rudra  and\n      Kunchukuttan, Anoop  and\n      Bhattacharyya, Pushpak","booktitle":"Proceedings of the 2019 Conference of the North {A}merican Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies, Volume 1 (Long and Short Papers)","month":"jun","year":"2019","address":"Minneapolis, Minnesota","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"https://aclanthology.org/N19-1387","doi":"10.18653/v1/N19-1387","pages":"3868--3873","abstract":"Transfer learning approaches for Neural Machine Translation (NMT) train a NMT model on an assisting language-target language pair (parent model) which is later fine-tuned for the source language-target language pair of interest (child model), with the target language being the same. In many cases, the assisting language has a different word order from the source language. We show that divergent word order adversely limits the benefits from transfer learning when little to no parallel corpus between the source and target language is available. To bridge this divergence, we propose to pre-order the assisting language sentences to match the word order of the source language and train the parent model. Our experiments on many language pairs show that bridging the word order gap leads to significant improvement in the translation quality in extremely low-resource scenarios."},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"nasa_report1","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Maynard, O. E. and Brown, W. C. and Edwards, A. and Haley, J. T. and Meltz, G. and Howell, J. M. and Nathan, A.","title":"Microwave Power Transmission Studies. Volume 1: Executive Summary","institution":"NASA","year":"1975","number":"19760008506"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"nasa_report2","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Maynard, O. E. and Brown, W. C. and Edwards, A. and Haley, J. T. and Meltz, G. and Howell, J. M. and Nathan, A.","title":"Microwave Power Transmission Studies. Volume 2: Introduction, organization, environmental and spaceborne systems analyses","institution":"NASA","year":"1975","number":"19760008507"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"nasa_report3","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Maynard, O. E. and Brown, W. C. and Edwards, A. and Haley, J. T. and Meltz, G. and Howell, J. M. and Nathan, A.","title":"Microwave Power Transmission Studies. Volume 3: Mechanical systems and flight operations","institution":"NASA","year":"1975","number":"19760008508"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"nasa_report4","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"Maynard, O. E. and Brown, W. C. and Edwards, A. and Haley, J. T. and Meltz, G. and Howell, J. M. and Nathan, A.","title":"Microwave Power Transmission Studies. Volume 4: Sections 9 through 14 with appendices","institution":"NASA","year":"1975","number":"19760008509"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"nguyen-etal-2017-reinforcement","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"71048ef8545afca1","fields":{"title":"Reinforcement Learning for Bandit Neural Machine Translation with Simulated Human Feedback","author":"Nguyen, Khanh  and\n      Daum{\\'e} III, Hal  and\n      Boyd-Graber, Jordan","booktitle":"Proceedings of the 2017 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing","month":"sep","year":"2017","address":"Copenhagen, Denmark","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"https://aclanthology.org/D17-1153","doi":"10.18653/v1/D17-1153","pages":"1464--1474","abstract":"Machine translation is a natural candidate problem for reinforcement learning from human feedback: users provide quick, dirty ratings on candidate translations to guide a system to improve. Yet, current neural machine translation training focuses on expensive human-generated reference translations. We describe a reinforcement learning algorithm that improves neural machine translation systems from simulated human feedback. Our algorithm combines the advantage actor-critic algorithm (Mnih et al., 2016) with the attention-based neural encoder-decoder architecture (Luong et al., 2015). This algorithm (a) is well-designed for problems with a large action space and delayed rewards, (b) effectively optimizes traditional corpus-level machine translation metrics, and (c) is robust to skewed, high-variance, granular feedback modeled after actual human behaviors."},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"original_chireix","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"71048ef8545afca1","fields":{"author":"Chireix, H.","journal":"Proceedings of the Institute of Radio Engineers","title":"High Power Outphasing Modulation","year":"1935","month":"nov.","volume":"23","number":"11","pages":"1370 - 1392","keywords":"","doi":"10.1109/JRPROC.1935.227299","issn":"0731-5996"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"original_eer","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"71048ef8545afca1","fields":{"author":"Kahn, L.R.","journal":"Proc. of the IRE","title":"Single-Sideband Transmission by Envelope Elimination and Restoration","year":"1952","month":"july","volume":"40","number":"7","pages":"803 -806","keywords":"","doi":"10.1109/JRPROC.1952.273844","issn":"0096-8390"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"output_cap_book","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"J. Vuolevi and Timo Rahkonen","title":"Distortion in {RF} Power Amplifiers","publisher":"Artech House Publishers","year":"2003","address":"685 Canton St. Norwood, MA 02062","edition":"1st","month":"Feb","note":""},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"pajic05_thesis","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"author":"S. Pajic","title":"Robust Design Methodology for Class-{E} Amplifiers for\n                  Microwave Applications","school":"University of Colorado at Boulder","year":"2005","type":"","address":"Boulder, CO","month":"","note":"http://charon.colorado.edu/microwave/theses/Pajic\\_thesis.pdf"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"papineni2002bleu","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"title":"Bleu: a method for automatic evaluation of machine translation","author":"Papineni, Kishore and Roukos, Salim and Ward, Todd and Zhu, Wei-Jing","booktitle":"Proceedings of the 40th annual meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics","pages":"311--318","year":"2002"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"peris-casacuberta-2018-active","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:31:15Z","response_hash":"71048ef8545afca1","fields":{"title":"Active Learning for Interactive Neural Machine Translation of Data Streams","author":"Peris, {\\'A}lvaro  and\n      Casacuberta, Francisco","booktitle":"Proceedings of the 22nd Conference on Computational Natural Language Learning","month":"oct","year":"2018","address":"Brussels, Belgium","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"https://aclanthology.org/K18-1015","doi":"10.18653/v1/K18-1015","pages":"151--160","abstract":"We study the application of active learning techniques to the translation of unbounded data streams via interactive neural machine translation. The main idea is to select, from an unbounded stream of source sentences, those worth to be supervised by a human agent. The user will interactively translate those samples. Once validated, these data is useful for adapting the neural machine translation model. We propose two novel methods for selecting the samples to be validated. We exploit the information from the attention mechanism of a neural machine translation system. Our experiments show that the inclusion of active learning techniques into this pipeline allows to reduce the effort required during the process, while increasing the quality of the translation system. Moreover, it enables to balance the human effort required for achieving a certain translation quality. Moreover, our neural system outperforms classical approaches by a large margin."},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"plate_and_grid","verdict":"verified","so